        <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Responsible person and service director details</h1>
        <p class="govuk-body">
          Before your organisation can take live payments, the GOV.UK Pay payment service provider carries out customer due diligence checks to meet UK anti-money laundering
          requirements.
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-body">
          As part of these checks, the payment service provider needs information about relevant directors or equivalent senior people responsible for the organisation's operations
          and governance.
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-body">To complete the checks, you need to provide details of:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
          <li>a responsible person</li>
          <li>a service director</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">The responsible person and service director need to be 2 different people.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">The payment service provider processes and stores the personal information you submit. GOV.UK Pay does not store it.</p>

        <p class="govuk-body">
          Providing personal information for these checks does not transfer your organisation's liability to the responsible person or service director. Liability remains with your
          organisation.
        </p>

        <p class="govuk-body">The checks on the responsible person and service director do not involve a hard credit search.</p>
        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Responsible person</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">The responsible person should be:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
          <li>authorised to sign contracts for your organisation</li>
          <li>senior enough to access relevant customer files and records</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">They also need to be:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
          <li>an employee of your organisation, not an external consultant</li>
          <li>able to decide independently whether to report suspicious activity or transactions</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">Examples of appropriate roles include:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
          <li>head of finance</li>
          <li>finance director</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">You need to provide the responsible person's:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
          <li>full name</li>
          <li>date of birth</li>
          <li>home address</li>
          <li>work phone number</li>
          <li>work email address</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">The payment service provider will use this information for:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
          <li>electronic identity verification</li>
          <li>sanctions screening</li>
          <li>politically exposed person (PEP) screening</li>
        </ul>
        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Service director</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">The service director needs to be either:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
          <li>the director responsible for the service</li>
          <li>another person at director level or in an equivalent position in your organisation</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">Examples of appropriate roles include:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
          <li>chief executive officer</li>
          <li>chief financial officer</li>
          <li>chief operating officer</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">
          For organisations that formally delegate authority to staff, the service director can be a staff member at director level or equivalent whose role is set out in the
          scheme of delegation.
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-body">You need to provide the service director's:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
          <li>full name</li>
          <li>date of birth</li>
          <li>home address</li>
          <li>work email address</li>
        </ul>
